00:02:45.779 --> 00:02:47.574
(upbeat music)

00:02:47.574 --> 00:02:50.720
Me trying to become a
partner at a Big Law firm.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.290
This little maneuver is gonna
cost us 51 years. (laughs)

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:58.610
Okay, this is funny probably only to me

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.070
and a handful of people in Big Law.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.620
So, all right, how do I explain this?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.420
Big Law tends to be very prestigious.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.728
It tends to be very well-paying.

00:03:07.728 --> 00:03:10.380
However, it takes a really long time

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.940
and a whole lot of work to
become partner in a Big Law firm.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.554
It varies, some of the smaller big firms,

00:03:17.554 --> 00:03:21.100
you can partner in six to 10 years.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.253
In some of the bigger big firms,

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:28.900
you might get in after 12
to 14 years if you're lucky.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.400
And a lot of these huge
firms have up and out

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.170
where if you don't make partner
on whatever track they have,

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:37.210
say it's after 10 years, you don't get in.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:38.967
You will never become a big firm partner.

00:03:38.967 --> 00:03:41.820
And some of these big firms let in

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:45.703
eight people into their
partnership a year.

00:03:47.177 --> 00:03:49.240
Don't get me started about this.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.490
Anyway, if you screw up one thing

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.886
and you're on the partner track,

00:03:52.886 --> 00:03:55.890
it's gonna cost you a
lot of time potentially.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.400
And this "Interstellar" clip (laughs)

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.810
that it might cost you 51 years.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.210
Dang, it really does feel like that

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.846
for some of these firms.

00:04:04.846 --> 00:04:06.630
(upbeat music)

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.960
Me going into the doc to
turn off tracked changes

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.010
and add Oxford commas

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.310
without the partner's knowledge. (laughs)

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:15.650
So, Microsoft Word is extremely pervasive

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.850
in the big firm world.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.740
And for some reason,

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:23.000
some of those partners out
there don't use Oxford commas.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.060
They're wrong.
(intense music)

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.870
They should be ostracized.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.100
But

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.240
look, sometimes, they are the boss

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.680
and you have to do what they say.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.840
So, it is a very
enterprising young associate

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.380
who goes in without tracking the changes

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.250
to change things to an Oxford comma,

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.800
hoping that the big firm partner

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.330
doesn't notice what you have done.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.610
I very much support that decision

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:48.010
because in Oxford comma,
everyone knows it,

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.839
the right way of doing things.

00:04:49.839 --> 00:04:51.630
(upbeat music)

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:53.410
Live look at class action attorneys

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:56.960
after reaching a settlement. (laughs)

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.740
Yeah, so, (laughs)

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.990
how do I say this without
offending everyone?

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.580
When you have a big class action verdict

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.280
or a big settlement,
there's a lot of money

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.680
because you're aggregating
lots and lots of small claims.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.740
So, a claim that might be
only $20 if you aggregate it

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.220
among a million different class members,

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.950
well that's $20 million.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:22.030
And the people that
really benefit from that

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:25.404
are of course, the class
action plaintiff's attorneys

00:05:25.404 --> 00:05:27.080
because they're gonna get a chunk of that,

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:30.710
maybe 30% of that chunk.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:31.700
And now, I happen to think

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.820
class-action lawsuits are very important.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:38.580
It really does make sure that
the violators of these laws,

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.623
whether it's a big
corporation or whatever,

00:05:40.623 --> 00:05:42.510
they actually do follow the law

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.343
because otherwise,

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.200
there would just be a whole bunch of small

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:47.520
infractions that no one

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:48.950
would have an incentive to take to court.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.160
So, class-actions serve
a very important purpose.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.480
That doesn't mean however,

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:53.700
that the class action attorneys

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.040
don't make a huge amount of money

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.273
when they get a nice fat settlement.

00:05:58.273 --> 00:06:00.180
(upbeat music)

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:01.640
There should be law school classes

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:03.410
about how to explain things clearly,

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.530
in non-legalese, to clients.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:07.360
Amen to that.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.110
Well, frankly, I made an
entire YouTube channel

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.950
devoted to basically
(laughs) exactly that.

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.880
So, if you're having
trouble explaining something

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.050
to your client, just
send them to LegalEagle.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.220
They'll tell you (laughs)

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.972
the non-legalese way of
thinking about these things.

00:06:22.972 --> 00:06:24.600
(upbeat music)

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:25.750
Okay, gonna tell my kids

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:28.260
this was Supreme Court justice
Sonia Sontomayor (laughs)

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.150
and Neil Gorsuch. (laughs)

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.570
The current controversy there

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:35.780
is reporting that Neil
Gorsuch refuses to wear a mask

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.980
around Sonia Sontomayor

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:42.840
despite the fact that she has
some preexisting conditions.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:46.910
But yeah, you can definitely
feel some not amused vibes

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.240
coming from Sophia Vergara here.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.381
That's probably what Sonya
Sontomayor is thinking

00:06:52.381 --> 00:06:54.852
even though she would never vocalize it.

00:06:54.852 --> 00:06:56.700
(upbeat music)

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.550
95% of lawsuits end up
getting settled like...

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.420
I'm gonna pay you a confidential (laughs)

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.070
sum to (beep) off. (laughs)

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:03.903
Yeah.

00:07:03.903 --> 00:07:05.040
Well, yes, on TV,

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.470
you see Harvey Specter's
in front of a jury

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.790
basically every day of the
week and twice on Sundays.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:12.110
That is not reality.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.430
It's actually more like 98% of all cases

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:15.950
settled before getting to trial.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.890
And yeah, I bet a good number

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:20.720
of those are in fact confidential.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:22.635
And a lot of those are for nuisance value.

00:07:22.635 --> 00:07:27.290
As this is hinting at in a
not particularly discreet way,

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:28.900
you're just paying off nuisance value

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:31.050
because it's not worth hiring attorney

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.600
to defend or whatever,

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.749
and it's just cheaper to pay 'em off.

00:07:34.749 --> 00:07:36.370
(upbeat music)

